<article class="env-lemma" id="022J">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/022J">Lemma <span data-tag="022J">34.12.1</span>.</a> Any set of big Zariski sites is contained in a common big Zariski site. The same is true, mutatis mutandis, for big fppf and big étale sites. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because the union of a set of sets is a set, and the constructions in Sets, Lemmas <a href="/tag/000J" data-tag="000J">3.9.2</a> and <a href="/tag/000X" data-tag="000X">3.11.1</a> allow one to start with any initially given set of schemes and coverings. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>